NOTICE
======

pi-ultrasearch bundles no third-party source in this repository. It drives a separately built
resident search daemon ("the UltraSearch engine") that is a **renamed fork** of an MIT-licensed
upstream project.

Upstream work
-------------

  Project : fsearch
  Author  : Noah Dunnagan
  URL     : https://github.com/noahdunnagan/fsearch
  Version : 0.2.1 (git tag v0.2.1, commit 88e63fd)
  Licence : MIT — Copyright (c) 2026 Noah Dunnagan
  Source  : pinned upstream checkout, default location ~/.cache/fsearch

The upstream licence text is reproduced verbatim in the engine working copy's LICENSE file and is
never modified by the rebrand. What the fork changes:

  * Cargo package/library/binary name: `fsearch` -> `ultrasearch`
  * default data directory: `Library/Application Support/FSearch` -> `.../UltraSearch`
  * default socket name: `fsearch.sock` -> `ultrasearch.sock`
  * install name and login-agent label, and user-facing help/version/error text

What the fork does **not** claim: authorship, copyright, or ownership of the upstream engine. The
rename is a local integration detail so that every user-facing name in this project is UltraSearch.

The rebrand is reproducible and idempotent:

    engine/rebrand.sh <upstream-checkout> <destination>

See `docs/engine-rebrand.md` for the build, install, migration and rollback procedure.

Third-party runtime dependency
------------------------------

`typebox` (MIT) is imported for tool parameter schemas and is provided by the Pi Agent host. It is
declared as an optional peer dependency and is not vendored here.
